        "id": 90772,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-14T02:03:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TheSoundOfTrees\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TheSoundOfTrees:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I enjoy games where Ra is fighting Dawn - I always imagine them bickering about WHO has the power of the sun…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>By the same token, Golem Unity vs. Omnitron for the future of machinekind…</p>\n<p>(It bothers me significantly that Omnitron's components are not Equipment cards, because villains aren't allowed to have Equipment.&nbsp; If Omnitron-X can Self-Sabotage his past self's Components, why can't he also Singularity them?&nbsp; Why can't normal Unity Bot-Fix them, when she can do it to the Staff of Ra or similar Relics?&nbsp; It makes perfect mechanical sense, it just bugs me on a flavor level.)</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
